sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Faculty Sender
    participant T as Trusted Public-Key Channel
    participant U as Untrusted Transfer Directory
    participant A as Attacker
    participant R as Examination Coordinator
    S->>S: Generate RSA-4096 pair; encrypt private PEM with password
    R->>R: Generate separate RSA-4096 pair; encrypt private PEM
    S->>T: Sender public key only
    T->>R: Pin trusted sender public key
    R->>T: Recipient public key only
    T->>S: Pin trusted recipient public key
    S->>S: Read bounded binary examination paper
    S->>S: Generate fresh 256-bit AES key and 12-byte nonce
    S->>S: Canonical metadata as AAD; AES-256-GCM encrypt; produce 16-byte tag
    S->>S: Recipient RSA-4096 OAEP; SHA-256 and MGF1-SHA256; label empty
    S->>S: Build canonical envelope; RSA-PSS SHA-256 and MGF1-SHA256; salt 32 bytes; sign all unsigned fields
    S->>U: Canonical JSON package with signature
    opt Adversary controls delivery
        U->>A: Encrypted package copy
        A->>U: Modify ciphertext, metadata, signature, nonce, tag or encrypted key
    end
    U->>R: Delivered package
    R->>R: Bound size; strict canonical JSON, schema, Base64 validation
    R->>R: Verify RSA-PSS with pinned sender public key
    alt Invalid signature
        R->>R: Reject; no plaintext saved
    else Valid signature
        R->>R: Check authenticated sender and recipient identifiers
        alt Wrong participant identity
            R->>R: Reject; no plaintext saved
        else Intended recipient
            R->>R: Unlock recipient private PEM; RSA-OAEP recover AES key; require 32 bytes
            alt Wrong private key or OAEP failure
                R->>R: Reject; no plaintext saved
            else Session key recovered
                R->>R: AES-GCM decrypt with identical canonical AAD
                alt Invalid GCM authentication
                    R->>R: Reject; no plaintext saved
                else All verification succeeds
                    R->>R: Validate safe destination; atomic plaintext publication
                    R->>R: Report signature and GCM verification success
                end
            end
        end
    end
    Note over S,R: Private keys never transmitted. Confidentiality uses AES-256-GCM and RSA-OAEP.
    Note over S,R: Integrity uses RSA-PSS and GCM; sender authentication uses the trusted sender public key.
